  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “5th Sunday after Pentecost” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, Jesus said to His disciples: Unless your justice abounds more than that of the scribes and Pharisees, you will not enter into the kingdom of heaven. You have heard that it was said to those of old: You shall not kill; and whoever kills will be subject to judgment. But I say to you that whoever is angry with his brother will be subject to judgment. And he who says to his brother, Raca, will be subject to the council. And he who says, Fool, will be subject to the Gehenna of fire. If, therefore, you offer your gift at the altar, and there you remember that your brother has something against you, leave there your gift before the altar, and go first and be reconciled with your brother; and then you shall come and offer your gift.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w024", "w025"], "anchor": "w024", "gloss": "it was said" }, { "words": ["w074", "w075"], "anchor": "w074", "gloss": "you remember" }] }
  },
